# The toolchain is LF-only: .prettierrc.json sets endOfLine "lf" and the .husky hooks are
# shell scripts. Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true yields CRLF working
# files that prettier rejects, which makes `bun run lint` — and so the pre-commit hook —
# impossible to pass. The stored blobs are already LF, so this pins existing behaviour.
* text=auto eol=lf

bun.lock -text
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
